[SIZE=6][B]MC Data Bridge - Release Notes (v2.2.2)[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=5][B]Overview[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Version 2.2.2 is a major release introducing enterprise-grade concurrency, integrity, and performance protections derived from an architectural security audit. Features include monotonic distributed lock fencing tokens, normalized snapshot SHA-256 integrity validation, single-transaction atomic saves, event-driven lock release messaging to eliminate pre-login latency, standard HMAC-SHA256 identity hashing, and automated unit testing in CI.[/SIZE]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]

[SIZE=5][B]Key Changes[/B][/SIZE]

[SIZE=4][B]🔒 Monotonic Distributed Lock Fencing Tokens (#41, AUDIT §2)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Epoch Fencing Protection:[/B] Added [CODE]lock_version[/CODE] ([CODE]BIGINT DEFAULT 0[/CODE]) to [CODE]player_data[/CODE]. Every lock acquisition increments [CODE]lock_version[/CODE], producing a monotonic fencing token.
[*][B]Stale Write Prevention:[/B] Saves, heartbeats, and lock releases evaluate [CODE]WHERE uuid = ? AND locking_server = ? AND lock_version = ?[/CODE]. Delayed servers or un-fenced post-GC pause writes are automatically rejected, protecting database state from stale session overwrites.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]🛡️ Normalized Data Integrity Checksums (#42, AUDIT §3)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Normalized SHA-256 Checksum Verification:[/B] Added [CODE]snapshot_checksum[/CODE] ([CODE]VARCHAR(64)[/CODE]) to [CODE]player_data[/CODE].
[*][B]Snapshot Integrity Verification:[/B] Computes canonical SHA-256 hashes across health, food, XP, NBT blobs (inventory, armor, ender chest, PDC), and game mode salted with [CODE]security.seed[/CODE]. Protects against database tampering across normalized component tables.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]⚡ Atomic Single-Transaction Persistence & Migration (#44, #45, AUDIT §5, §6)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Single-Transaction Component Saves & Releases (#44):[/B] [CODE]saveAndReleaseLockComponents[/CODE] now executes all component writes ([CODE]databridge_inventories[/CODE], [CODE]statistics[/CODE], [CODE]metadata[/CODE], [CODE]companions[/CODE], [CODE]maps[/CODE]) and lock releases within a single database connection and transaction ([CODE]setAutoCommit(false)[/CODE] ... [CODE]commit()[/CODE]).
[*][B]Transactional Legacy Migration (#45):[/B] [CODE]loadLegacyData[/CODE] executes component migration and legacy [CODE]data = NULL[/CODE] clearing inside a unified transaction with automatic rollback ([CODE]rollback()[/CODE]) on failure to eliminate dual-source-of-truth conditions.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]⚡ Event-Driven Lock Release Messaging — 🚀 Up to 10X Faster Server Switching (#46, AUDIT §9)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]⚡ Up to 10X Faster Cross-Server Transfers:[/B] Dispatches an instant [CODE]LockReleased[/CODE] plugin message upon source server save completion. Destination servers wake up waiting pre-login threads immediately, slashing server-switch lock wait latency from [B]~500ms down to a near-instant ~50ms[/B]!
[*][B]Resilient Fallback:[/B] Retains 500ms database polling loops as a zero-downtime fallback mechanism if network messages are dropped.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]🔐 Keyed HMAC-SHA256 Identity Verification (#47, AUDIT §12)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Standard HMAC-SHA256:[/B] Upgraded identity hashing in [CODE]HashUtils[/CODE] to use standard [CODE]HmacSHA256[/CODE] key derivation with [CODE]security.seed[/CODE].
[*][B]Seamless Dual Verification:[/B] Automatically verifies existing records against both HMAC-SHA256 and legacy salted SHA-256 digests for 100% backward compatibility without table migrations.
[/LIST]

[SIZE=4][B]🧪 Automated CI Unit Testing & Concurrency Suite (#43, AUDIT §16)[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]CI Test Automation:[/B] Re-enabled automated unit testing in GitHub Actions ([CODE].github/workflows/maven.yml[/CODE]) on pull requests and merges.
[*][B]Concurrency & HMAC Unit Tests:[/B] Added [CODE]LockFencingTest[/CODE] and [CODE]HashUtilsTest[/CODE] verifying lock token increments, stale write rejections, HMAC generation, legacy fallback, and null safety.
[/LIST]

[CENTER]----------------------------------------------------------------[/CENTER]
[I]For installation instructions and configuration details, please refer to the README.md and config.yml.[/I]
